33,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It appears that our previous projects have been most successful when the resulting spaces were open for general booking, whereas those limited to a single wing were poorly rated. Also, older blocks contain hazardous materials that have caused significant delays.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings align with Toshio's point on utility; general-purpose rooms are in constant demand while specialist rooms often sit idle. Furthermore, taking rooms out of service has forced us to pay for expensive off-site replacements.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,George,,"I've found that while we have some technicians with spare hours, our front-of-house and grounds staff are severely under-resourced. More concerningly, bench technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks that should be automated.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My research shows that projects based on comfort or appeal often slip by a year or more, while those driven by inspection findings stay on track. Additionally, weather has caused six weeks of losses on exposed work.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, mechanical and ducted plant costs have risen by a fifth, while surfacing remains stable. I also discovered that we have no renewal reserve for audiovisual equipment bought in previous rounds.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Given the hazardous materials in older blocks and the poor ratings for restricted-use spaces, we should prioritize a project that is both broadly accessible and avoids complex structural surprises.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,I agree. We must also consider the cost of off-site replacements; any plan that takes essential rooms out of service for an extended period will create a significant financial burden.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,George,,"I am particularly concerned about the bench technicians. If we can implement a solution that removes those manual burdens, it would provide much-needed relief to our remaining staff.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"We must be cautious about any project that is purely for ""appeal,"" as those are the most likely to slip. A project driven by necessity or inspection findings would be far more reliable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are caught between a rock and a hard place; the very mechanical upgrades that could relieve George's technicians are precisely the ones seeing the sharpest price increases.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Perhaps we should look for a middle ground—a project that addresses a clear necessity to ensure timely delivery, but remains open to the wider campus to maximize its rating.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"That would be ideal. If we can find a project that doesn't require extensive room closures or off-site hiring, we can avoid the financial drain I discovered.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,George,,I must insist that we don't overlook the technicians' plight; a project that automates their manual routines would be a tangible victory for staff welfare.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we prioritize a project based on a technical necessity, like an inspection finding, we can mitigate the risk of the schedule slipping, which has been a recurring issue.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,And let us not forget the audiovisual gap; any plan involving new media facilities would be a hollow victory if we have no reserve to maintain the equipment.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I believe we have a clear set of criteria now: we need a project that is a technical necessity, serves a broad user base, and avoids the pitfalls of older block partitions.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. We must prioritize a plan that balances high demand for general space with a minimal impact on our current timetable and budget.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,George,,"I still believe the most urgent need is to alleviate the manual burden on our technicians, provided we can manage the costs Benjamin mentioned.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with George's concern, but we must ensure the project is framed as a necessity rather than a luxury to avoid the scheduling delays I've observed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are in agreement on the parameters. Let us see which of the candidates best fits this delicate balance of necessity, accessibility, and financial realism.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
