59,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Looking at the candidates, the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade addresses the technicians' manual burdens and is a technical necessity, though we must be mindful of the rising costs for ducted plant.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"The Central Study Commons would satisfy the high demand for general-purpose rooms and likely receive high post-occupancy ratings, though we must consider the cost of temporary room replacements.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,George,,"The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade is the only option that directly solves the technicians' manual routine issues, which I believe is a critical priority for our staff's well-being.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The Campus Path Network is exposed to the weather, which my research shows causes significant delays, and the Media Production Center risks the same audiovisual funding gap Benjamin noted.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Central Study Commons is a safe bet financially, but the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade, while expensive, addresses a systemic failure in our current infrastructure that we can no longer ignore.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"While the Study Commons is appealing, the ventilation upgrade is a necessity that avoids the hazardous material risks of older blocks if handled correctly, and it serves a critical function.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"I must point out that the Study Commons involves converting a ground-floor hall, which might trigger the hazardous material delays Toshio mentioned, making the ventilation upgrade a more predictable choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,George,,"Exactly. The ventilation upgrade is a direct response to a technical failure, which Mizuki noted is the most reliable way to ensure the project actually finishes on schedule.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. If we frame the ventilation upgrade as a necessary infrastructure correction, we avoid the scheduling slips associated with ""appeal"" projects and provide a concrete benefit to the staff.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure to see us align so quickly; the ventilation upgrade is the only choice that transforms a technical liability into a functional asset for our staff.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I believe we have reached a consensus; the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade satisfies our requirements for necessity, staff relief, and scheduling reliability.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I concur. It avoids the risks of the other options and addresses a fundamental need without the uncertainty of general-purpose room conversions.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,George,,I am fully satisfied with this choice; it is the only plan that truly acknowledges the hard work of our technicians.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. It is the most pragmatic choice, ensuring we deliver a necessary improvement without falling into the trap of unrealistic timelines.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, it is the most logical conclusion. We shall proceed with the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade, accepting the market costs in exchange for operational stability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I cast my vote for Candidate A, the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
